# To-Do List Manager

## Overview

A console-based Java application that allows users to manage a simple to-do list through an interactive menu. Users can add tasks, view all tasks, remove completed tasks, and exit the program.

## Features

- Add new tasks to a to-do list
- View all current tasks
- Remove tasks by selecting their number
- Menu-driven interface with repeated user interaction until exit
- Input validation for menu selections

## Concepts Practiced

- ArrayLists
- Loops (`do-while`)
- Conditional Statements
- Methods
- User Input with `Scanner`
- Menu-Driven Program Design

## Files

- `ToDoListManager.java`

## Sample Menu

```text
======== TO-DO LIST MANAGER ========
1. Add a Task
2. View All Tasks
3. Remove a Task
4. Exit
```

## Skills Demonstrated

- Building interactive console applications
- Managing dynamic collections using `ArrayList`
- Processing user input and validating choices
- Organizing program logic into clear menu options
